WEBVTT

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:03.740
Thank you.

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:59.860
What I am, it's a man I know

00:02:00.670 --> 00:02:05.290
Evil men do not bring your evil here.

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:12.270
I warn you, beware the wrath of one thing.

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:20.670
450 megawatts, that's it.

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:24.070
Two degrees per minute, no more.

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:29.980
Curse the spinal fluid, 35 cc.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.080
No more, no less.

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:33.200
Precise measurements are critical at this stage.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:33.720
Good.

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:35.670
Dr. Arcane, may I say something?

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:37.830
Graham, get that bloody thing out of my face, will you?

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:38.910
Sorry, sir.

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:42.640
I just want to say that being a witness to this,

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:44.540
being a small part of your victory,

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.390
makes me feel very honored.

00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:47.370
Well, of course it does, Graham.

00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:51.010
You there, make sure there are no bubbles in that mannitol broth

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:51.990
before you integrate it.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:54.480
I mean to think that after all these years of research,

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:56.320
you have finally discovered the key

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:58.480
to decoding the secrets of human aging.

00:02:59.530 --> 00:02:59.970
Thank you, sir.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.060
Thank you so much for putting it in perspective for me, Graeme.

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:06.150
What about the other night?

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:29.660
Take it from here.

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:31.940
This is it, Graham.

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:35.200
I'm poised on the very threshold of scientific glory.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:37.360
Activate molecular separators.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:40.300
Where's the ancillary power, Graham?

00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:41.880
It should kick in automatically.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:42.900
Well, it hasn't.

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:44.100
I can't have a power dip.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:44.680
Not now.

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:47.070
Man, backup systems are not in space.

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:47.990
Damn it!

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:11.000
Unbelievable. This can't be happening. My entire bloody experiment's ruined, Graham. Get me engineering. Heads will roll for this.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:15.220
But, Doctor, first the engineers will pay, then the rest of these morons!

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:59.870
So as did they suffer in the end, engineers especially needed anyone.

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:02.300
yet, Doctor. Why the hell not?

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:04.810
I thought you might enjoy doing it yourself.

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:07.450
Do I look like I'm capable of having

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:09.590
any fun at all at this present time, Graham?

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:16.540
No, sir. But while I know that

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:18.720
this is a terribly disappointing setback for you,

00:05:18.740 --> 00:05:21.090
I want you to know that I stand ready

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:22.770
to help you rebuild

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:26.050
the experiment. The remains

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:28.150
of my brilliant formula were destroyed

00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:29.550
in that awful lab accident.

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:33.700
Well, actually, Doctor, I don't think it was an accident.

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:36.390
I believe it was sabotage.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:38.580
Sabotage? By whom?

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:41.700
That's a little hard to explain.

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:43.100
Don't play with me, man!

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:45.070
Absolutely, sir.

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:48.140
You see, we weren't the only ones in the complex tonight

00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:49.780
who experienced strange event.

00:05:50.440 --> 00:05:53.560
There were reports of unexplained lights and sounds

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:55.450
and a drop in temperature.

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:57.370
Just tell me who is responsible.

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:59.170
They'll pay dearly for it, I promise you.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.500
Not who, but what.

00:06:01.780 --> 00:06:05.530
I believe we were assaulted by poltergeists.

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:10.210
Poltergeists, and they call me mad?

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:12.790
Have you been taking your medication lately, Graham?

00:06:12.950 --> 00:06:14.070
I don't believe in ghosts.

00:06:14.410 --> 00:06:16.350
There's been quite a bit of empirical data

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:19.200
to support the idea of restless spirits.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:22.600
Besides, I can prove it.

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:29.140
Tape was made from the security cameras from the main gate.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:36.520
The lights you see here are luminescent protoplasmic particles, fairly common in poltergeist infestations.

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:38.420
You're wasting my time.

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:43.850
Any number of vents could be responsible for those lights, including a malfunctioning electrical system.

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:47.010
That's why I took the liberty of analyzing the tape's audio track.

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:51.380
Gibberish.

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:55.230
Listen to what happens when it's been digitally enhanced at variable speeds.

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:08.940
know better. I'd say that was General Sunderland. But he's dead. Killed when his headquarters

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:14.380
self-destructed. Disintegrated by a series of powerful explosions a year ago. That's true,

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:21.620
Graham. I was visited by a poltergeist. More than one, I'd say. Imagine that cranky old

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:27.710
buzzard and a few of his spirit friends in this very room. It's incredible. My point

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:29.970
exactly. And incredible is my...

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:33.630
middle name after all my words Graham this could be one of my most

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:37.870
astonishing discoveries to date life after death well actually doctor I was

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:42.580
kind of hoping well that we might well that we might share the credit on this

00:07:42.580 --> 00:07:46.610
because after all I did all the preliminary work on this on my own

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:52.970
unsupervised you heard him Graham he didn't say Graham did he Graham no he

00:07:52.970 --> 00:07:57.500
said RK I want you it is me they're trying to contact Graham and to hell

00:07:57.500 --> 00:07:59.930
with this bloody experiment if I'm to be

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.140
denied the secrets to immortality, so be it.

00:08:02.470 --> 00:08:04.070
I shall contact General Sunderland,

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:06.210
get instructions for mastering the hereafter.

00:08:06.430 --> 00:08:07.290
This is marvelous, Graham.

00:08:08.110 --> 00:08:09.490
Absolutely bloody marvelous.

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:17.300
Yeah, marvelous.

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:56.680
Sunderland

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:00.970
Anton Arcade.

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:03.420
You here?

00:09:04.780 --> 00:09:06.620
Graham said there were rumors of a haunting.

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:08.120
No offense.

00:09:10.670 --> 00:09:12.190
Come out, come out, wherever you are.

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:18.560
Holland, blazes are you doing here?

00:09:18.890 --> 00:09:20.890
I know why you're here, and I want you to leave.

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:22.360
You always want me to leave.

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:24.940
There are forces here you can never understand.

00:09:25.260 --> 00:09:27.100
I'm a scientist, I like a bit of a challenge.

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:28.660
So if you'll excuse me.

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:29.880
For once, listen.

00:09:31.530 --> 00:09:34.090
The energies of life and death are out of balance.

00:09:34.430 --> 00:09:36.570
I sense something violent waiting for you.

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:38.960
Really? Something violent?

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:42.180
Perhaps I'll call Graham and have him check it out.

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:33.820
All right, Holland, if this is your idea of making a point, consider it done.

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:41.380
Now what?

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:02.460
I know you're out there somewhere.

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:07.170
Saw you on television, General Sunderland.

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:10.020
You look quite good under the circumstances.

00:11:11.840 --> 00:11:14.420
I heard you. You asked for me.

00:11:45.670 --> 00:11:51.900
As long as it isn't the headless horseman.

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:55.540
Fire, Tom.

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:03.580
General?

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:56.330
Please confirm.

00:13:00.190 --> 00:13:13.470
General Sunderland, if you're here, give me a signal.

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:16.920
One knock for yes, two knocks for no.

00:13:25.380 --> 00:13:26.240
Knocks? What does that mean?

00:13:27.940 --> 00:13:28.200
Me.

00:13:52.460 --> 00:13:59.920
Remember I did not you activated the self-destruct and your complex not

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:04.020
You shot me with a razor and left me for dead.

00:14:31.310 --> 00:14:33.330
There's no escape, Arcade.

00:14:34.660 --> 00:14:41.280
Best part about being dead is I can do more damage to you now than I ever could when I was alive.

00:14:41.660 --> 00:14:48.290
Let alone some friends.

00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:01.600
Ha, ha, ha, ha.

00:15:34.380 --> 00:15:37.600
Holland, I knew you'd come. You've got to do something.

00:15:38.090 --> 00:15:40.230
The spirits are upsetting the balance of nature.

00:15:40.450 --> 00:15:42.650
Yeah, well, they're not doing much for me either. Help me!

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:45.940
They're not of this world. I have limited power over them.

00:15:49.770 --> 00:15:50.610
Do something, Holland!

00:16:30.540 --> 00:16:58.690
you when i need you i've been hurt i need some help step in the light so i can see you i don't

00:16:58.690 --> 00:16:59.830
think that's such a terribly good idea

00:17:01.760 --> 00:17:05.450
Look here, I'm Anton Arcane.

00:17:05.570 --> 00:17:09.920
Is that on your shirt? Blood.

00:17:12.160 --> 00:17:12.380
Okay.

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:14.210
Now what's really...

00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:19.980
Don't do this, General. All I want to do is be your ally.

00:18:20.840 --> 00:18:24.200
What did I ever do to you but give you loyal service and brilliant performance?

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:27.100
You lived and I didn't.

00:18:27.740 --> 00:18:29.780
Well, you kidnapped my wife.

00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:31.740
And all I ever wanted was to have her back.

00:18:32.220 --> 00:18:33.800
I wanted her for myself.

00:18:34.260 --> 00:18:35.700
I deserved her.

00:18:36.440 --> 00:18:38.400
That's an unrealistic ambition on your part.

00:18:38.620 --> 00:18:40.280
You could hardly hold that against me.

00:18:40.580 --> 00:18:45.500
What I hold against you, Arcane, is just a matter of fairness.

00:18:49.200 --> 00:18:51.960
It is about to be all evened up now.

00:19:11.450 --> 00:19:13.750
Do you want to know a little secret arcane?

00:19:14.030 --> 00:19:17.330
Do you want to know what happens when people die?

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:22.880
All the pain they ever inflicted on others.

00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:35.580
Fasten your safety belts.

00:19:37.080 --> 00:19:47.740
You must not run from them.

00:19:48.260 --> 00:19:49.640
You must defeat the Polar Geists.

00:19:50.300 --> 00:19:51.860
Brilliant, Holland. Do you mind telling me how?

00:19:52.200 --> 00:19:53.480
Only way may be with heat.

00:19:53.850 --> 00:19:55.490
Their protoplasm energy is fragile.

00:19:56.050 --> 00:19:57.430
You may be able to incinerate them.

00:19:57.630 --> 00:19:59.630
Oh, that's marvelous. How do I do that?

00:20:03.160 --> 00:20:05.390
It's full of fuel.

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:14.870
You're a Sunderland bat.

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:36.920
So, he survived after all.

00:21:38.410 --> 00:21:39.190
We're Sunderland.

00:21:39.870 --> 00:21:42.150
He and the other spirits have returned to their world.

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:46.340
And it worked. I did it.

00:21:47.460 --> 00:21:49.160
Once again, the swamp is in balance.

00:21:50.170 --> 00:21:51.030
Thanks to me.

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:55.510
Once again, your ego claims deeds done by others.

00:21:56.610 --> 00:21:57.650
What, did I miss something?

00:21:58.950 --> 00:21:59.970
Or did I blow up the sh...

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:02.760
Yes, Holland. It's marvelous.

00:22:03.680 --> 00:22:06.150
The swamp is indebted to me.

00:22:08.170 --> 00:22:13.300
Not really. I would think about that for a while. A long, long while.

00:22:21.900 --> 00:22:27.330
Of all the mysteries in the swamp, none are more perplexing than when mortal enemies are forced to work together.
